{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a highly diastereoselective and enantioselective photoredox pinacol coupling of aromatic aldehydes. This is achieved using a red-absorbing organic dye (dimethoxyquinacridinium, DMQA+) as a photocatalyst in combination with titanium complexes (Cp2TiCl2 or chiral SalenTiCl2). The system uses Hantzsch's ester as a sacrificial reductant and orange light (590 nm) to selectively reduce Ti(IV) to Ti(III), which then promotes the coupling with high D,L (syn) selectivity.",
